## 2. Mathematical Models & Kinematics

### 2.1 Differential Drive Vehicle Kinematic Model
The vehicle pose in world coordinates is defined as $\mathbf{q} = [x, y, \theta]^T$. The differential drive kinematics with wheelbase $L$ and wheel radius $R$ are:

$$\begin{bmatrix} \dot{x} \\ \dot{y} \\ \dot{\theta} \end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix} \cos\theta & 0 \\ \sin\theta & 0 \\ 0 & 1 \end{bmatrix} \begin{bmatrix} v \\ \omega \end{bmatrix}$$

Where forward linear velocity $v$ and angular velocity $\omega$ relate to individual wheel linear velocities $(v_L, v_R)$ by:

$$v = \frac{v_R + v_L}{2}, \quad \omega = \frac{v_R - v_L}{L}$$

Inverse kinematics for motor actuation:

$$v_L = v - \frac{\omega L}{2}, \quad v_R = v + \frac{\omega L}{2}$$

### 2.2 5-Channel Ultrasonic Sensor Spatial Transformation
Each ultrasonic sensor $i \in \{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\}$ is mounted at fixed offset $d_{off,i}$ from the vehicle centroid at relative mounting angle $\beta_i \in \{-90^\circ, -45^\circ, 0^\circ, +45^\circ, +90^\circ\}$.

The world coordinate of an obstacle hit detected at range $r_i$ is computed as:

$$\alpha_i = \theta + \beta_i$$

$$\begin{bmatrix} x_{hit,i} \\ y_{hit,i} \end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix} x + d_{off,i} \cos\theta + r_i \cos\alpha_i \\ y + d_{off,i} \sin\theta + r_i \sin\alpha_i \end{bmatrix}$$

### 2.3 Ground Plane Inverse Perspective Projection
For an obstacle pixel centroid $(u, v)$ with bounding box base $v_{base}$ on an image of width $W$, height $H$, and camera focal length $f_{pix}$:

$$d_{forward} = \frac{h_{cam} \cdot f_{pix}}{\max(v_{base} - v_{horizon}, \epsilon)}$$

$$d_{lateral} = \frac{u - W/2}{f_{pix}} \cdot d_{forward}$$

$$\begin{bmatrix} x_{obs} \\ y_{obs} \end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix} x + d_{forward}\cos\theta - d_{lateral}\sin\theta \\ y + d_{forward}\sin\theta + d_{lateral}\cos\theta \end{bmatrix}$$

### 2.4 Dynamic 2D Cost Grid & Continuous Gaussian Inflation
The cost grid $C(x, y) \in [0.0, 1.0]$ is updated dynamically:

$$C(r, c) = C_{static}(r, c) + \max_{i} \left( \mathbb{I}_{\{d_i \le R_{lethal}\}} \cdot 1.0 + \mathbb{I}_{\{R_{lethal} < d_i \le R_{total}\}} \cdot \exp\left( -3 \cdot \left(\frac{d_i - R_{lethal}}{R_{inflation}}\right)^2 \right) \right)$$

Temporal decay for dynamic obstacles:

$$C_{t}(r, c) = C_{static}(r, c) + \gamma \cdot (C_{t-1}(r, c) - C_{static}(r, c)), \quad \gamma = 0.92$$

