## 3. Communication Protocols

### 3.1 MATLAB $\rightarrow$ Main ESP32 (USB Serial @ 115200 Baud, LF terminated)
| Packet Format | Description | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `SET_MOTORS,<pwmL>,<pwmR>` | Sets direct PWM speed for left and right motors ($-255$ to $255$) | `SET_MOTORS,160,120` |
| `FORWARD,<speed>` | Drives forward at specified PWM duty | `FORWARD,150` |
| `BACKWARD,<speed>` | Drives backward at specified PWM duty | `BACKWARD,120` |
| `LEFT,<speed>` | Turns left differential | `LEFT,140` |
| `RIGHT,<speed>` | Turns right differential | `RIGHT,140` |
| `STOP,0` | Active motor brake | `STOP,0` |
| `EMERGENCY_STOP` | Hard safety override brake | `EMERGENCY_STOP` |
| `PING` | Communication heartbeat watchdog refresh | `PING` |
| `RESET_ENC` | Clears hardware encoder tick counters | `RESET_ENC` |

### 3.2 Main ESP32 $\rightarrow$ MATLAB (USB Serial @ 20 Hz)
| Packet Format | Description | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `US,L:<d>,FL:<d>,F:<d>,FR:<d>,R:<d>` | 5-channel ultrasonic distances in centimeters | `US,L:140.2,FL:95.0,F:48.5,FR:110.0,R:150.0` |
| `ENC,<leftTicks>,<rightTicks>` | Cumulative hardware encoder pulse counts | `ENC,1240,1238` |
| `STATE,<state>,PWM:<lPWM>,<rPWM>` | Real-time vehicle operating state & active PWM | `STATE,FORWARD,PWM:150,150` |
| `WARN,<warningType>` | Proximity or system warnings | `WARN,OBSTACLE_AHEAD_48.5` |

### 3.3 ESP32-CAM $\rightarrow$ MATLAB (HTTP Wi-Fi Endpoint)
* `GET http://<ESP32-CAM-IP>/capture`: Returns single full-resolution JPEG frame for frame-by-frame MATLAB image processing.
* `GET http://<ESP32-CAM-IP>/stream`: Standard multipart MJPEG video stream.
* `GET http://<ESP32-CAM-IP>/status`: Returns JSON device health status, RSSI, and streaming FPS.
* `GET http://<ESP32-CAM-IP>/flash?state=1`: Controls on-board LED illumination for night road navigation.

